<title>PORTUGAL: Yield falls on Portugal 3-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Portugal 3-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management auction of 25 billion escudos of three-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>ISSUER: Republic of Portugal</p>
<p>MATURITY: 23 Mar 2000</p>
<p>AMOUNT PLACED: 9.125 bln esc</p>
<p>COUPON: 5.375</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 5.501315</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 5.51  LOWEST: 5.44</p>
<p>DEMAND: 66.16 bln esc</p>
<p>PAYMENT FREQUENCY: Annual</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 175.38 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
</text>
